acme_onboard: Hi CS + infra, new customer integration hitting throttle during warmup. Using go-sdk v0.9.7, 12 instances (k8s HPA), each runs a prefetch on start. At ~180 rps sustained we see a wave of 429s to /v1/embed. Any quick fixes?

liz_cs: Sorry you're blocked. Can you paste the init snippet and whether you're using ephemeral creds or long-lived keys? Also what's your preflight pattern (every start or per-request)?

acme_onboard: Long-lived project key for now. Init:```go
client := redwood.NewClient(os.Getenv("RW_KEY"))
// each pod calls client.Prefetch(context.Background()) on boot
```We call prefetch on every pod start (no splay).

devin_platform: That aligns with a preflight stampede. Two short mitigation steps: 1) add a startup splay (0-8s) so pods don't preflight in lockstep, 2) enable client-side preflight cache (client.Options.EphemeralCache = true) so token reuse reduces load. On our side I can enable preflight-coalescing for your org for 20m.

felix_se: Add this retry wrapper to catch 429s and back off with jitter:```go
func doWithRetry(ctx context.Context, fn func() error) error {
  backoff := 150 * time.Millisecond
  for i:=0;i<6;i++{
    if err := fn(); err==nil { return nil }
    if apiErr, ok := err.(redwood.APIError); ok && apiErr.Status==429 {
      jitter := time.Duration(rand.Intn(int(backoff)))
      time.Sleep(backoff + jitter)
      if backoff < 10*time.Second { backoff *= 2 }
      continue
    }
    return err
  }
  return fmt.Errorf("max retries")
}
```Also set HTTP2 keepalive and max connections so requests reuse channels (client.Options.KeepAlive=true, MaxConns=8). That usually drops concurrent preflight traffic.

ops-bot: preflight_coalesce flag enabled for tenant acme_onboard until ts=1718082400.

acme_onboard: Quick test after toggling EphemeralCache and adding 0-8s splay + keepalive: 429s dropped to near-zero. Sample log:```log
[1718081132] prefetch: cache miss uid=abc -> fetched
[1718081140] prefetch: cache hit uid=abc token_age=22s
[1718081152] embed:200 size=1024 latency=180ms
```Thanks!

liz_cs: I'll follow up with a short runbook: recommended SDK knobs (EphemeralCache=true, KeepAlive=true, MaxConns=8, startup_splay=0-10s), backoff template, and an ops checklist to request a preflight quota bump if you expect large simultaneous boots. Do you want the preflight_coalesce flag kept on for another day while you upgrade to go-sdk v0.9.9?

acme_onboard: Yes please keep it on 24h. We'll schedule a canary of v0.9.9 tomorrow; plz ping if we need help. Thanks everyone :pray:
